  her buy nothing group formula question  mark baby is not doing well on breast  milk the response overwhelmed her when i  got home my front porch and inside was  full of formula i had like two or three  months worth of supply from at least 15  people it really shows that you know  you're never alone it's okay to ask for  something and you know be loved on by  people  buy nothing has spread to almost 7 000  communities across more than 40  countries the pandemic fueled a spike in  membership more than a million and a  half people joined and the number taking  part in buying nothing groups now tops 5  million worldwide are the by nothing  groups on the internet one of the last  kind corners sometimes it feels like  that to me and i think because in a by  nothing community you you know that  you're speaking literally to your  neighbors with record inflation and the  stresses of the pandemic by nothing  became for some a financial and  emotional lifeline  it really brings joy to others but  honestly brings more joy to yourself  helping others and you know it's good to  receive too and build a community it is  really worth doing for cbs morning's  janet chamleon the woodlands texas  it feels great it feels great to give  people things uh and also particularly  with kids stuff yeah wear it like two  times like a winter coat yeah it's great  to just hand it pass it on down the line  giving is a love language that everybody  is fluent yeah yeah we can all speak it  you're so right about that nate i like  the my favorite line the piece where she  says it can show that you're never alone  no matter what you were going through  and how isolated you feel right there's  somebody that's feeling that that's  right it's a good reminder of that  that's true janet thank you

